The lesson learned is that the small gain showed the value of catalyst-driven entries,

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:13.800
but also highlighted how quickly momentum can stall without sustained volume.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:20.180
The rule extracted from that trade states always require volume confirmation above the 20-day

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:26.240
average before entering momentum trades on earnings beats. That filter now applies directly

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:31.840
to names like Dell. Now let us cover two tools and techniques that support today's approach.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:38.680
Portfolio Visualizer is a free web platform that lets users run historical backtests on custom

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:45.960
portfolios using ETF and stock data going back decades. Canadian investors can compare a TFSA mix

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:52.080
of sector ETFs against the TSX composite to quantify potential alpha before committing capital.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:59.140
Access the back testing module with no login required for basic use. If today's ROIC screen

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:04.820
interests you, this tool shows exactly how those names performed in past macro slowdowns.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:11.840
Prediction market data via predicted or polymarket APIs aggregates crowdsource probabilities

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:18.640
on events such as policy deals or rate paths. Pulling the API feed into a simple spreadsheet

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:23.800
gives retail traders a real-time gauge of market implied odds versus their own thesis.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:30.220
The edge comes from spotting divergences between prediction prices and traditional analyst forecasts

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:36.720
before they converge. Both tools require only a few minutes to set up yet add measurable discipline.

