00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:08.240
Our AI analysis continues to learn from the volume confirmation pattern and is adjusting entry filters

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:14.220
accordingly. Now here is something that most retail investors get wrong and it cost me money

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:20.540
before I figured it out. Imagine you bought a consumer staple ETF last week when recession headlines

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:26.560
first hit. Your order filled at the quoted price yet the real mechanics between click and execution

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:33.040
often include hidden costs that erode the margin of safety buffet demands. Buffet evolved from

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:38.080
Benjamin Graham's cigar butt bargain hunting to Charlie Munger's emphasis on quality

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:44.380
compounders with durable economic modes. Key principles include staying inside a defined circle

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:50.500
of competence, insisting on a margin of safety before purchase and treating index funds as the default

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:57.660
for most investors who lack time or edge. His notable wins such as Coca-Cola and Apple illustrate

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:04.080
the power of long-term ownership of predictable cash flow machines. Professionals always verify

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:09.660
whether a business can earn above its cost of capital for 10 plus years before committing capital.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.400
The biggest misconception is that Buffet style investing means only buying cheap assets.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:21.340
Instead, always demand both quality and price discipline before entering any position.

